<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n86315" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρευμεν-ής</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ές</span>, 
			contr.
		 fr. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρηϋμενής</span> (v. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πραϋμενής</span>), <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>soft of temper, gentle, gracious,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινι</span> to one, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ag.</u>
				840
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Hec.</u>
				538
			</span></i>: abs., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἴδοιτο . . πρευμενοῦς ἀπ᾽ ὄμματος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Supp.</u>
					210(207)
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀχαιῶν πρευμενεστέρων τύχοις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Tr.</u>
					739
				</span></i>
			. 
			Adv., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρευμενῶς αἰτεῖσθαι,
				παραινέσαι,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Pers.</u>
				220
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				224
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δέχεσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Eu.</u>
					236
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> of events,
				<i>favourable,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατελθὼν . . πρευμενεῖ τύχῃ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Ag.</u>
					1647
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τελευτὰς . . πρευμενεῖς κτίσειεν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Supp.</u>
					140
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρευμενοῦς . . νόστου τυχόντας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Hec.</u>
					540
				</span></i>
			 (s.v.l.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>propitiating,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χοαί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pers.</u>
					609
				</span></i>
			.</div>
